ually classes although there  isn't a huge difference between them to  be fair you'll definitely need to pick a  character you like the voice of because  they do like to talk back for blood has  introduced one new thing to evolve the  series  cards by building a deck of cards we  each have a range of buffs to adapt how  we fight it could mod our health pool  maybe a damage buff too this introduces  replayability which should keep the game  going strong after halloween ends and  horror games are forgotten back for  blood wants to eat your brains on  october 12th on the playstations the  xboxes and the pcs  how do you feel about superhero movies  what about a marvel game which has  absolutely nothing to do with the movies  here's marvel's guardians of the galaxy  a single-player action adventure in  which we play a star lord guardians has  a ton of light rpg elements with  abilities that must be earned and  unlocked and leveled up to their fullest  the weapons you choose do actually  matter as certain enemy types have  certain weaknesses to certain elements i  said certain a lot there making freeze  blasters the right choice in some  scenarios and the worst choice in others  as starlord we control our team and  order them to perform moves and the  better you become the more you will  churn out combos starting with groot and  chaining through all the other members  of the team to make it look like a  complete badass in addition to combat  exploration plays a part in the story  building as do world puzzles and to keep  the whole thing together banter plays  the most important part the dialogue  these guys turn out because they never  shut up constant banter just like you'd  expect from this ragtag misfit squad  guardians of the galaxy is here to  marvel you on october 26th on ps4 ps5  the xboxes and pc and there's a switch  version which i presume will be a  cloud-based experience  okay let's go for some free games for  the month and they are super retro first  up any undertale fans in the house the  legend of undertale was continued in  deltarune a few years back and all of a  sudden last week chapter 2 suddenly  arrived totally for free if you aren't  an undertale fan these visuals may not  flow to your boat but those of you who  want more from tony fox especially his  musical abilities can now play both  deltarune chapter one and chapter two  completely free on ps4 switch and pc  there's no voice acting here the story  is all written so you best get used to  reading and that story is cut up with  small boss battles which are essentially  bullet hell demanding the player to  avoid contact with fast-moving objects  this is added to with a turn-based final  fantasy combat approach which focuses on  timing so if you like undertale you  should play this and it's free in it bro  a quick note about another free game  coming soon blood hunt a vampire focused  battle royale which was announced during  the sony event in september and is 100  going to be released before 2022 so not  long left i wasn't going to talk about  it this month because i didn't think it  would release but it's the time of the  year where vampires are quite cool so  it's potentially going to drop this  month a vampire focused battle royale on  playstation 5. don't hold me to this but  i presume this is the deadline they were  looking for when they announced that  title was coming if not i'll talk about  it in november as a replacement for that  free game take this one another battle  royale just look at it though it's all  retro super animal royale okay what you  see is is what you get but as a release  from the more hardcore battle royale  games out there super animal royale is  downright dumb fun running people over  in a hamster ball is surprisingly fun  and the twin stick shooting mechanics  work really well so if you're looking  for some silly fun a game which probably  won't last you very long but it's still  worth a try and it's quite a small  download file 